   "date": "2018-03-27T20:43:05Z",
   "subject": "Re: change legend order of ggplot in python",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>When the numbers are converted to to factors they are made into characters and sorted by that. <br><br></div>Easiest way is to make it a factor and supply the levels. Something like: <br><span><br></span></div><div><span>library(tidyverse)<br><br></span></div><div><span>my_data_frame %&gt;% <br></span></div><div><span>mutate(label = factor(label, levels = 1:19) %&gt;%<br></span></div><div><span>ggplot(., aes(x=x, y=y, colour = label) + geom_line()</span><br><br><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
